The Muon Optimizer

Muon (Jordan et al., 2024) has recently been proposed to optimize neural network weights representable as matrices. At iteration $t$, given current weight $\mathbf{W}_{t-1}$, momentum $\mu$, learning rate $\eta_{t}$ and objective $\mathcal{L}_{t}$, the update rule of the Muon optimizer can be stated as follows:

\displaystyle\mathbf{M}_{t} \displaystyle=\mu\mathbf{M}_{t-1}+\nabla\mathcal{L}_{t}(\mathbf{W}_{t-1}) \displaystyle\mathbf{O}_{t} \displaystyle=\text{Newton-Schulz}(\mathbf{M}_{t})\text{} \mu\mathbf{M}_{t}+\nabla\mathcal{L}_{t}(\mathbf{W}_{t-1}) \mathbf{M}_{t} \displaystyle\mathbf{W}_{t} \displaystyle=\mathbf{W}_{t-1}-\eta_{t}\mathbf{O}_{t}

